rows.en:
"I'm sorry, I'm sorry."
She apologized to each wilted flower, one by one, as she desperately tended them.
In the rain, forgetting the passing of time, forgetting even her own serious illness, she tended the flowers with all her heart, on and on and on.{p}

The red hydrangeas offered in front of the grave turn an even deeper red.
They're beautiful hydrangeas, dyed a red so bewitching there's nothing else like it in this world.
That's the end of my story.{p}

"Hurry up and open it.
My hands are going numb."
"Hang on, it hardly ever gets used, so the door sticks."{p}

"Ando, what's wrong?"
"Stop it, stop it!"
Ando hit Koyama with the chair he was holding.{p}
